{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1549228-what-will-change-if-we-remove-mage-sight-subsystem","id":1549228,"title":"What will change if we remove mage sight subsystem?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-13T02:28:58-07:00","id":1549228,"title":"What will change if we remove mage sight subsystem?","content":"Recently, we've started our first MtA campaign. While I really enjoy the magic system and the way it is structured, I'm really bothered with a subsystem around Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Scutiny and Revelations rolls worked extremely anti-climatic at our table. When confronted with a truly bizzare phenomenon, players seemed really engaged. With repeated rolls, handing over pieces of information, it just became a slog.<br /> <br /> My main issue is that the subsystem is completely non-interactive. You just roll and wait, and as a GM, I had the additional burden of coming up with more meaningful chunks. Among four players scrutinizing, it just killed the moment. I did my best to put some colour in the descriptions and normally they work fine, so I don't think that's the issue.<br /> <br /> What would break if we just replace scrutiny with a single roll, giving away information based on the number of the successes?<br /> <br /> Specifically, I was thinking of the following solution: Normally, to break a mystery of rank n, roughly n^2/2 successes are needed with k^2 dice, where k is the pool, so I just thought of replacing it with a single roll with rank/2 + 2 being the treshold (+2 to factor in wp) and with mana giving additional dice at the rate 1m/1d, but with the risk of making the mystery more complex, as usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T15:15:02-07:00","id":1549264,"title":"","content":"You would lose the ability to parse out the details of the Mystery in cool symbolic visions, since some might be too complex to solve in one go. If you use Revelation and Scrutiny to give you a place to start, you have a big plot hook that will be in the back of the cabal's mind.<br /> <br /> Maybe they have linked Opacity and you need to fully Scrutinize another Mystery to uncover it. <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> goes into this in more detail.<br /> <br /> Remember that both take a turn and there is the penalty for mundane actions, meaning you can challenge your players via complications. Car chases, windows of opportunity, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}